From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HarnessOS <patches@harnessos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: retain worker dispatch authority and recovery

Upstream stopped minting the per-dispatch capability (#23994), so the argv start
neither mints nor bakes one: it still builds the preamble before the pane exists,
pre-allocates the handle and commits the launch token, then binds through
upstream's prepareStartingWorkerAuthority with the launch-token commitment
required to match. The failed-start identity copy is upstream's, as is the OMP
bracketed-paste idle case (omp-readiness-transcripts.test.ts covers it with a
captured screen).

On v1.4.222 the host measures whether the typed launch line can carry its prompt
whole (upstream #24257, startup-line-prompt-carry) and starts the agent clean
when it cannot. The argv start asks for that verdict through onStartupPromptCarry:
a carried brief keeps the paste-free start, and an uncarried one is pasted through
upstream's readiness settlement once the agent holds the terminal, so the
launch-token bind stays and no worker is reported ready without its brief.

Carried-Because: Preserve the deployed Orca fork concern on v1.4.222.
Tests: Declared unit and integration gates in components/orca/build.toml.

